<article class="env-example" id="08RH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08RH">Example <span data-tag="08RH">7.33.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category endowed with the chaotic topology (Example <a href="/tag/07GE" data-tag="07GE">7.6.6</a>). For every object $U_0$ of $\mathcal{C}$ the functor $u : U \mapsto \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _\mathcal {C}(U_0, U)$ defines a point $p$ of $\mathcal{C}$. Namely, conditions (1) and (2) of Definition <a href="/tag/00Y5" data-tag="00Y5">7.32.2</a> are immediate as the only coverings are given by identity maps. Condition (2) holds because $\mathcal{F}_ p = \mathcal{F}(U_0)$ and since the topology is discrete taking sections over $U_0$ is an exact functor. </p>
</article>